+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve the site (default port: 11222).
+
+The site uses native CSS in `styles.css`; no build step is required. It targets
+modern browsers with support for cascade layers, CSS nesting, and `@scope`.
+
+The cascade order is declared up front: `reset`, `tokens`, `base`, `layout`,
+`components`, then `accessibility`. Keep new rules inside a named layer so
+unlayered declarations do not unexpectedly override the architecture.
+
+Palette primitives feed semantic tokens such as `--color-brand` and
+`--color-surface`. Shared spacing, typography, radii, motion, and layout values
+live in the token layer. Component-specific values, such as `--hero-image`,
+are declared on their owning component.
+
+Layout, component, and accessibility rules are scoped to `.daily-grind`.
+Components use explicit classes and shallow native nesting; `:where()` keeps
+element defaults low in specificity. Use component classes for new markup,
+and keep presentation out of HTML style attributes. Logical properties support
+different writing directions. Interactive styles include keyboard focus and
+reduced-motion preferences.
